Spon wrote:
>  "jim.etchi...@gmail.com" <jim.etchi...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>> > You really need some form of magic resistance, or you'll likely fall
>> > prey to some horrible instadeath incidence.

This is one of the evil genius features of Nethack.  You tend to need MR
at the Castle.  The way to get guaranteed MR is in the Castle after
you've mostly cleared it.

>> Good point. My +6 cleaver works quite nicely and I have werebane for
>> off-hand.
>
> Cleaver is 2-handed so you can't use that with another weapon (or with
> the shield).  You can't put an artifact in your off-hand (try it and
> see), which is annoying because it pretty much means that Werebane is
> way less useful than a non-artifact saber.

Werebane has the advantage that if you got it as a gift it opens your
saber skill slot.  Until you have a better artifact it's no worse than a
regular silver saber.  Cleaver is one of many better artifacts,
arguably.

> I'd go for Vorpal and a
> long sword/katana/silver dagger/silver spear given what you've told me
> you've got.  At a pinch, I guess an elven broadsword or dwarfish spear
> would do well in the off-hand too, but I've never had to use either of
> those myself. 

Elven broadswords are plentiful in the game and are high on the list for
damage among non-artifact weapons.  Long sword and silver saber are
comparatively less common but one of them is guaranteed in the game in
the initial inventory of the watch captain in mine town.  I've lost my
pet to the watch captain's long sword and ended up using an elven
broadsword as my secondary wield in a fair number of games over the
years.  It isn't a long strategy that I use as I replace it when I start
encountering barrow wights or Nazguls but it works fine in the short
run.  A strategy that does not apply to this game - Elven broadsword
exercises the broadsowrd skill slot so for chaotic characters who start
out able to enhance it that prepares for Stormy the chaotic crowning
gift.


